The bills is a list of 5, 5, 5, 10, and 20.
The fives is 0, while the tens is 0.
The valid is 1.
For each bill in bills.
If bill is 5, add 1 to fives.
If bill is 10 and fives is 0, set valid to 0.
If bill is 10 and fives is more than 0, subtract 1 from fives, add 1 to tens.
The paid is 0.
If bill is 20 and tens is more than 0 and fives is more than 0, subtract 1 from tens, subtract 1 from fives, set paid to 1.
If bill is 20 and paid is 0 and fives is at least 3, subtract 3 from fives, set paid to 1.
If bill is 20 and paid is 0, set valid to 0.

If valid is 1, show true, otherwise show false.
